    {
      "id": "89a4d4474d591dafa2df9982475de194807beee8",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1781769385,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Coverity is returning\n\n```\n*** CID 1592166:  Memory - corruptions  (OVERRUN)\n/builds/wireshark/wireshark/epan/dissectors/packet-pldm.c: 548 in ver2str()\n542     \t} else {\n543     \t\tc_offset += snprintf(buf_ptr+c_offset, VER_BUF_LEN-c_offset, \"-\");\n544     \t}\n545     \t// Update\n546     \tif (update != 0xff) {\n547     \t\tc_offset += snprintf(buf_ptr+c_offset, VER_BUF_LEN-c_offset, \".\");\n>>>     CID 1592166:  Memory - corruptions  (OVERRUN)\n>>>     Calling \"print_version_field\" with \"buf_ptr + c_offset\" and \"12UL\" is suspicious because \"buf_ptr\" points into a buffer of 12 bytes and the function call may access \"(char *)(buf_ptr + c_offset) + 11UL\".\n548     \t\tc_offset += print_version_field(update, buf_ptr+c_offset, VER_BUF_LEN);\n549     \t} else {\n550     \t\tc_offset += snprintf(buf_ptr+c_offset, VER_BUF_LEN-c_offset, \"-\");\n551     \t}\n552     \t// Alpha\n553     \tif (alpha != 0x00) {\n\n** CID 1592165:  Null pointer dereferences  (NULL_RETURNS)\n/builds/wireshark/wireshark/epan/prefs.c: 2653 in column_hidden_fmt_set_cb()\n```\n\nWould it make sense to use a wmem_strbuf here instead?",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1789689689",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-02-20T17:07:00.749Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-02-20T17:13:47.898Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 282964512,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 14451,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1781779016,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Maybe.  I missed out the -c_offset there.\nAlso was going to check whether should have buffer one longer than length passed into snprintf() so that it'll always be null-terminated.  Don't think it can be > 10 chars.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
